/// fields loses a signed, non-default `order`, and canonicalization re-encodes
/// from the decoded message, so the CID cannot be restored and verification
/// fails there. A decoder that RETAINS unknown fields may instead re-encode
/// identical bytes and match the CID — so passing the CID check proves nothing
